{"meta":{"ticker":"SPYD","as_of_date":"2026-10-02","performance_as_of":"2026-09-30","generated_at":"2026-10-03 08:45:39"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"SPYD","fund_name":"State Street SPDR Portfolio S&P 500 High Dividend ETF","category":"US Large-Cap Value","issuer":"State Street","index_name":"S&P 500 High Dividend Index","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0007,"aum":7192343663,"holdings_count":81,"inception_date":"2015-10-21","overall_score":4.09068117021277,"overall_rank":724,"sector_diversification_score":7.35347399731376},"description":{"tsi_description":"SPYD seeks to provide a high level of current dividend income by tracking the performance of the 80 highest-yielding stocks in the S&P 500 Index in equal weight. It differs from many competing high-yield ETFs in that it includes REITs, which means not all dividend income received counts as Qualified Dividend Income, or QDI, for U.S. tax purposes. Nevertheless, SPYD often offers one of the highest yields in the U.S. Equity ETF space, is broadly diversified at the company and sector levels, and has a cheap 0.07% expense ratio, which means most of the underlying income the fund receives flows through to its shareholders.","strategy_steps":["SPYD tracks the S&P 500 High Dividend  Index, which aims to hold the 80 highest-yielding securities in the S&P 500 Index, subject to certain constraints.","Based on each security's indicated dividend yield, or IAD, the top 64 are automatically selected for inclusion in the Index.","The remaining 16 securities are selected based on their IAD rank order, provided they rank within the top 96.","The Index is equal-weighted, which means target weights for each holding is approximately 1.25% at each semi-annual rebalance at the end of each January and July.","The S&P 500 Index itself has profitability requirements for new entrants, but the S&P 500 High Dividend Index applies no additional 